A||||5||porkchop||buying a fiero||||1||
Z||000000||porkchop||12-17-2001||07:37 PM||||I have been passing a gas station for a few months now that has a mint 88 gt. I pulled in and the mechanic ststed that the lady is looking to get rid of it for 3500. Body is mint - interior clean - seat has rip- still has original sterio. Can any one tell me if the price is good ? Moter has 120,ooo needs tires - has big rims and spoiler - fast back? Is this a decent price? What are major things to look for - what can go wrong --big <BR>Bob   ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||12-17-2001||07:53 PM||||A 13 year old car with 120K miles on it, almost anything COULD be wrong with it.  You would have to start it up and drive it.  $3500 seems a bit pricy unless the mechanics are in good shape.||||reg||1
Z||000002||avengador1||12-17-2001||09:13 PM||||You should be able to get it for less, but check it out carefully first. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||GTDude||12-17-2001||11:49 PM||||You guys are obviously afraid of the miles.  Is it a city car or a country car or what.  If it's a country car, it's just getting broken in.....IF it was maintained properly.  Personally it sounds like a killer deal to me if the body and paint really are mint.  I'd have a mechanic I trusted check it out.  I've been a mechanic for 25 years and I can usually drive a car around the block and tell you if it's worth buying.....not always....but usually.  But the point is...have someone knowledgeable inspect it before you buy it.  I paid 3,500 for my 86 GT with flawless paint and interior and 135,000 miles.  There is absolutely nothing wrong with the car.  It belonged to a collector who was getting older and was selling all his cars.  I think I got a deal.  Everything stock I turned a 7.62 0 to 60 today.  I'm not saying that I got an average car for a fair price.....im saying i got a fantastic car for a fair price.  That's what he needs to look for.  If it's an 88 and in the kind of shape that mine is in....it's worth 6k.  But that is yet to be determined.  Good luck!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DSCF0003a.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FIERO JOHN-WI||12-18-2001||08:35 AM||||Hey Porkchop, the mileage shouldn't be really something to worry about 120K, 13 years old, that mean 9,230.7692 miles a year,the national average is 15 to 17K a year, so heres what I would check, either a collector owned it(which I doubt, since things are worn out SEAT) it's been hit(which you'll see) or it's has alot of engine or tranny trouble. Once you find that out, then look in the trunk pockets under the carpet to see if they are rusty, then pull off the battery cover and check if the battery tray is rusty, then make sure the car HAS NOT been run, start it up and check to see if the exhaust manifolds are cracked (especially the back one) if the car is warmed up you won't know unless it's real bad crack. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||REDHOTT88||12-18-2001||09:39 AM||||Porkchop, Welcome to the Forum...<P>These guys are right. I just wanted to add, that the price seems a little high, maybe you could talk them down some. If not, it's up to you, check everything out, (of course it's not going to be perfect,) and if you really want a Fiero, buy it.<P>Any problems, you can always find the answer here!<P> <P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">       <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed </FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1">(Runs smooth, shifts crisp, red and shiny all over!)</FONT>||||reg||1
